add("Aether Blood", "Potion", "Rare", 0, "A glowing purple liquid. For 1 hour after you drink it, a spell slot you use counts as 1 level higher when setting the level the spell is cast at. A spell with no extra effect at higher levels gains nothing. Drink it a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum 1) and you become addicted. You must drink it again every 24 hours or have Disadvantage on Constitution checks and saves. The addiction ends with greater restoration or after 30 days without it.")
add("Arc Rifle", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0, "A rifle with glass tubes of sparking lightning, built by gnome engineers and illegal in most lands. It has 4 charges and regains 1d4 at dawn. Lightning Torrent: spend 1 charge as an action to fire a 60 ft line, 5 ft wide. Each creature in it makes a Dexterity save against your scatter save DC, taking 6d6 Lightning damage on a failure and half on a success. When you spend the last charge, roll a d20. On a 1 the rifle burns out and is useless.", ch=[4, "1d4", "dawn"])
add("Breath of Beleth", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, "An airborne poison that conjures the victim's worst fears, breathed in to take effect. Inhaled: a creature makes a DC 15 Constitution save or is Poisoned for 1 minute. While Poisoned it is Frightened of every hostile creature it sees and must Dash away from them by the safest route each turn, unless it has nowhere to go.")
add("Collar of Undead", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0, "Put it on a Large or smaller humanoid that died within the last 10 days and it returns to life with 1 hit point as undead. It needs no food, sleep or air. At dawn each day its hit point maximum drops by 1d4, and at 0 hit points it falls to dust. While it wears the collar it obeys you. As a bonus action you can give it an order. With none it repeats the last order and defends itself. If the collar is taken off, the creature drops to 0 hit points at once.")
add("Dreams Leaves", "Potion", "Uncommon", 0, "A drug from a magically grown plant. Whoever consumes it falls into a trance for 1 hour and counts as unconscious. On waking, with its dreams and glimpses of its possible future, it gains 1 dream point. Being attacked or shaken ends the trance early with no point. It can spend the point as a reaction to gain Advantage on one attack roll, ability check or saving throw. Using it addicts you. You must consume it every 24 hours or have Disadvantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma checks and saves. The addiction ends with greater restoration or after 30 days without it.")
add("Full Moon Extract", "Potion", "Uncommon", 0, "A powder that brings a surge of strength. For 1 hour after you take it, your Strength is 19 (if lower) and you have Advantage on Strength checks and saves. Take it a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier plus 1 (minimum 1) and you become addicted. You must take it every 24 hours or have Disadvantage on Dexterity checks and saves. The addiction ends with greater restoration or after 30 days without it. If you take it while addicted, make a DC 6 Charisma save or you attack the nearest living creature you see until the effect ends.")
add("Greatsword of the Craven", "Weapon", "Rare", 1, "A greatsword with a +1 bonus to attack and damage. While attuned you gain 5 ft of speed and Advantage on initiative. It is cursed, and attuning extends the curse to you. You will not part with it and keep it on you. You have Disadvantage on attack rolls with any other weapon. When you try to pick up another weapon it shifts away, so you make a DC 10 Dexterity check or spend an action to grab it.", by="a cowardly spirit", fx={"atk": 1, "dmg": 1}, base=["Greatsword"])
add("Thought Talker Orbs", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 1, "Two small orbs, an emitter under half an inch across and a receiver. A creature holding both touches them together as an action to activate them. Then any creature that enters or starts its turn within 5 ft of the emitter makes a DC 13 Wisdom save. On a failure, an attuned creature holding the receiver learns its surface thoughts.")
add("Shadow Steel Blades", "Weapon", "Very Rare", 1, "Any melee weapon except a club, flail, greatclub, light hammer, mace, maul, morningstar, warhammer, whip or quarterstaff, made of Shadow Steel. It is forged from souls and hits with spiritual pain. You have Advantage on attack rolls against a target in medium or heavy armor. A creature you hit makes a DC 14 Constitution save or is Stunned until the end of its next turn.", base=["Longsword"])
